# One repo per line:  /path/to/repo | stack:<type>
#
# stack-type is the KEY IDEA: ledger decisions are scoped to a kind of codebase,
# not a repo name. A tool can be right for one stack and wrong for another, and
# the verdict transfers to the next repo of the same kind.
#
# This file is gitignored — the paths are yours. Copy from this example.
/path/to/frontend-app   | stack:next-vercel
/path/to/erp            | stack:erp-supabase
/path/to/research       | stack:data-science
/path/to/strategies     | stack:trading
